---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Privacy" description="Mail goes directly to Google. No telemetry, no ads, no Sift server." path="/privacy">
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>Sift stores your mailbox on your Mac and collects no telemetry. Mail goes directly to Google; optional update checks go to GitHub.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What leaves your Mac</h2>
    <p>Mail traffic goes only to Google, directly over TLS — the requests needed to read, sync and send your mail. Two other network paths exist, and neither is hidden:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Remote images.</strong> Sift does not load an image a sender hosts on their own server by default: the account's remote-content policy decides, and a new installation starts at <code>ask</code>, which fetches nothing on its own. <code>block</code> never fetches anything external.</li>
      <li><strong>Update checks.</strong> Sift asks GitHub for the newest release manifest when it launches, so it can tell you a newer version exists. <strong>Settings → Updates</strong> turns the automatic check off, and the check by itself never downloads or installs anything.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>There is no Sift backend, no analytics endpoint, no crash reporter, and no ads.</p>

    <h2>What stays on your Mac</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A local SQLite database with your mailbox, search index, attachments, and drafts.</li>
      <li>Your Gmail app password or OAuth refresh token, stored in the macOS Keychain.</li>
      <li>Logs and diagnostics, which are written locally and never uploaded.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Remote images</h2>
    <p>An image a sender hosts on their own server is not fetched by default. A new installation keeps the account's remote-content policy at <code>ask</code>, so nothing external loads on its own; <code>block</code> never loads external content, and <code>allow</code> loads the HTTPS images a message needs without asking. Fetching a remote image would tell its sender that you opened the message, which is why it is not the default here.</p>

    <h2>Credentials</h2>
    <p>Sift authenticates with an app password or an OAuth refresh token. Tokens are held in the Keychain and only ever sent to Google. The local database never stores them.</p>

    <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
    <p>Removing an account deletes its Keychain entry and every row associated with it in the local database. Uninstalling the app and deleting its application support folder removes everything else.</p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>Open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/AadiXC0DE/Sift">GitHub</a> if anything here is unclear.</p>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
